"AI Computer Vision": {"1": "Today, {nama} learned about Computer Vision - how computers can 'see' and understand images. {nama} used the OpenCV library to explore image processing, blurring, and image editing techniques.", "2": "In this session, {nama} learned what a CNN (Convolutional Neural Network) is and how it helps computers recognise images. {nama} was also introduced to TensorFlow, a tool for training AI models.", "3": "Today, {nama} learned how to collect datasets for computer vision projects. {nama} used TensorFlow's dataset tools and data augmentation, then built a Horse and Human Classification project.", "4": "In this class, {nama} used a pre-trained AI model to build a face detection app - first for photos, then for live video.", "5": "Today, {nama} learned about the SSD (Single Shot Detector) model and used it to build an Object Detection app that can identify objects in both images and video.", "6": "In this session, {nama} explored the difference between Object Detection and Object Tracking. {nama} also learned about Euclidean Distance Tracker, contour detection, and image thresholding.", "7": "Today, {nama} applied the Euclidean Distance Tracker to track moving objects, assigned unique IDs to each detected object, and added visual markers to the tracked items.", "8": "{nama} reviewed all previous lessons and completed the mid-term exam.", "9": "In this class, {nama} learned about OCR (Optical Character Recognition) and used the EasyOCR library to build an Automatic Number Plate Recognition (ANPR) system.", "10": "Today, {nama} explored another use of OCR - recognising handwritten text - and used a pre-trained Keras model along with image processing techniques to make it work.", "11": "In this session, {nama} was introduced to MediaPipe, a powerful library for detecting body landmarks. {nama} used it for holistic tracking and built a Virtual Painter project.", "12": "Today, {nama} found the exact positions of hand landmarks using the enumerate() method, set up selection and drawing modes in the Virtual Painter, and finished the project using video frame masking.", "13": "In this class, {nama} learned about Face Mesh in MediaPipe, drew facial landmarks on a face, and built a fun Pig Face Filter project.", "14": "Today, {nama} explored more facial areas in MediaPipe and built a Dragon Face Filter project, including creating a Face Mesh class to detect specific facial regions.", "15": "In this session, {nama} learned how to detect whether a mouth is open or closed and used video masking to apply filter effects to each frame in real time.", "16": "{nama} reviewed all lessons and completed the final exam for this unit."},
"AI Machine Learning": {"1": "Today, {nama} learned about the relationship between AI, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning. {nama} also explored how Machine Learning works and practised using Pandas to manage data.", "2": "In this session, {nama} learned how Classification works in Machine Learning. {nama} prepared the Iris Flower dataset and visualised it using the Seaborn library.", "3": "Today, {nama} learned how the KNN Classifier algorithm works. {nama} trained a model, evaluated it, tuned its settings, and made predictions using the trained model.", "4": "In this class, {nama} was introduced to Natural Language Processing (NLP) - how computers understand human language. {nama} explored NLP with ChatGPT and practised using the NLTK library in Python.", "5": "Today, {nama} explored the steps involved in Sentiment Analysis and learned about Feature Extraction and Vectorization. {nama} started building a Spotify Review Sentiment Analysis project.", "6": "In this session, {nama} learned how Random Forest and Naïve Bayes classifiers work, improved model accuracy, and made predictions using the sentiment analysis model.", "7": "Today, {nama} applied NLP to a new project - Fake News Detection. {nama} also compared Classification and Regression models and learned how Logistic Regression works.", "8": "{nama} reviewed all previous lessons and completed the mid-term exam.", "9": "In this class, {nama} learned about Time Series Forecasting - predicting future values based on past data. {nama} built a Population Prediction project using Linear Regression.", "10": "Today, {nama} explored how Sales Forecasting works and built a Sales Prediction project using Plotly for data visualisation and Feature Engineering techniques.", "11": "In this session, {nama} learned about Rolling Windows, Exponentially Weighted Moving Average, Logarithmic Transformation, and Neural Networks. {nama} then made predictions using a neural network model.", "12": "Today, {nama} was introduced to Unsupervised Learning and K-Means Clustering. {nama} built a Customer Segmentation project using these techniques.", "13": "In this class, {nama} learned how Recommender Systems work - both content-based filtering and collaborative filtering - and built a Course Recommendation System.", "14": "Today, {nama} learned about Anomaly Detection using the Isolated Forest algorithm and applied it to a Credit Card Fraud Detection project.", "15": "{nama} reviewed all lessons and completed the final exam - including a written test and coding exam.", "16": "Today, {nama} continued and submitted the coding exam."},
"Android Developer": {"1": "Today, {nama} was introduced to React Native - a tool for building mobile apps. {nama} learned about View, Text, and Button components, and how to arrange them on screen.", "2": "In this session, {nama} learned how to style app layouts using Layout Style, Box Model, and Text Style, and practised using the TouchableOpacity component.", "3": "Today, {nama} learned how to use Flex layout to organise app screens. {nama} also added Image and ScrollView components to their project.", "4": "In this class, {nama} explored ImageBackground, Text Input, Opacity, Props, and Reusable Components - tools for building efficient and flexible app layouts.", "5": "Today, {nama} added a custom font and icons to their app and built a 'Popular' layout for the interface.", "6": "In this session, {nama} was introduced to React Native Hooks. {nama} practised using useState, useEffect, and setTimeout, then built a 'Guess the Country' screen.", "7": "Today, {nama} learned about Stack Navigation - moving between screens in a mobile app - and explored another way to use the useEffect Hook.", "8": "{nama} reviewed previous lessons and completed the mid-term exam.", "9": "In this class, {nama} learned how FlatList and StyleSheet work in React Native. {nama} then built the Home Screen for a Movie Collection app.", "10": "Today, {nama} explored Horizontal FlatList, learned how to add components before and after a list, and practised sorting data.", "11": "In this session, {nama} learned about the Ternary Operator and how to combine StyleSheet with Inline Style. {nama} continued building the Movie Collection app.", "12": "Today, {nama} learned how to send data from one screen to another and how to receive it. {nama} then built the Movie Detail Screen.", "13": "In this class, {nama} learned how to display the top 3 results, show an empty state message when there's no data, and add columns to a FlatList. {nama} built the Most Viewed Movie Screen.", "14": "Today, {nama} learned how to customise the header in Stack Navigation and built the Recommended Movie Screen.", "15": "{nama} completed Part 1 of the Android Apps Development exam.", "16": "{nama} completed Part 2 of the Android Apps Development exam."},
